  "rationale": "The throughput constraint (>=50 MSPS) requires 1 result/cycle, which only pipelined and pipelined_m provide (iterative and unrolled_k produce 1 result every N or ceil(N/k) cycles, so their throughput is Fmax/N which would need Fmax > 50*N MHz, implausible). The accuracy constraint max_abs_err <= 2^-20 requires sufficient data_width and n_iter; W=20-24 with N=20-26 should cover this. I focus the entire budget on these two families since they are the only feasible ones. pipelined gives the baseline area/power; pipelined_m explores the FF-reduction trade-off. The reserved front-mapping phase will sweep these ranges to map the Pareto front well. I allocate budget 50/50 between the two families to cover both the fully-pipelined and partially-pipelined trade-offs."
